 you're always going to have you  know bad apples in the system you're  going to have people who commit crimes  you're going to have people who are  hostile but as a general matter I think  what separates America from a lot of  other countries at least historically is  that the people tend to get along pretty  well we tend to trust each other and and  I noticed this growing up you know I  took a few trips when I was younger went  to Europe for example with my family and  on a school trip and you'd notice  differences in the culture where there  was a lot of distrust people did not  feel the same sense of cohesion and in  America look who we have a place where  we will have a bookstore and the books  will be outside of the store you know  they trust no one's gonna walk by and  and snatch one of the books and and take  it home and I think that stems from our  culture of Liberty and and when you are  you know self-reliant when you when you  demand personal responsibility in your  life you tend to trust each other  more actually when you put so much power  in governments hands you tend to become  distrustful of people do you feel do you  feel then there's a kind of broader  libertarian culture in America that is  related I mean it's the place we get  along because things are voluntary or  people are only showing up because I  want to I think that just our culture  from the very beginning from our  foundation was very much a classical  liberal trusting sort of culture where  people just work together in communities  there was very much of a community  sentiment and worked together to get  things done on a voluntary basis you  know maybe it stemmed from you know our  opposition to the throne at the very  beginning and and just the sense of  community hey we don't have a king  ruling over us we have to work together  the people you've mentioned that you  know we're in a period and you know  certainly Donald Trump reflects us and  helps further it but of animosity anger  what not what what can be done to kind  of start pulling that back and  recreating the the world that you're  talking about I think it requires a lot  of small steps and it requires different  people to do different things depending  on what their position and life is I you  know I'm in a position where I'm a  member of Congress I have a lot of  influence I feel the need to go out  there and use that that influence that I  have to spread the message of love  spread the message of Liberty talk about  working together and respecting each  other and how a lot of our problems can  be solved voluntarily we don't need  government to control everything and  decide everything for us and then when  we talk about government we can also  talk about different levels of  government that do things you know a lot  of people say well either government  will do it or the private sector and I  like to point out look there are  different levels of government to some  things might happen at the federal level  some things might happen at the state  level some things might happen locally  some things might happen in your family  there all sorts of government but when  you get closer to home it's it's like a  more like a private action and so  recasting it that way getting people to  understand what creates a you know a  smoothly operating society is important  to me what how are your constituents  responded are they happy with you did  they feel cheated because they elected  you as a Republican what what kind of  feedback have you been getting it's been  overwhelmingly positive now there are  definitely people who are upset they're  definitely people who are diehard Trump  supporters or very much you know  diehard party loyalists who who don't  like it but overall the reception has  been very positive and I think most  Americans are pretty independent minded  most Americans have very libertarian or  classical liberal tendencies and so I  think they can relate to my frustrations  working within the party system and why  I'd want to leave that that system  did you talk directly with your  constituents about this beforehand or  how did you but how did you manage that  well communication the important thing  to know about my district is that for  years I've been a very  independent-minded congressman people  know that I don't tell the party line  people know that when I run for office  I'm running as an independent principled  person I tell them the set of principles  I'm running on and they know that I'm  going to follow those principles even if  it means going against my party so  nobody's surprised by that kind of thing  and I think just all the interactions  I've had over the years I've held many  town halls I've been very open with the  community about where I stand and I've  listened to their concerns it was pretty  obvious to me that this is a community  that will be supportive of this kind of  thing do you worry about being primaried  and you know I've seen some early polls  showing that you you know you are gonna  have a real tough pre-election battle  yeah so I'm running as an independent so  I won't be involved in the primary but I  was never really worried about the  primary I mean if I'd stayed as a  Republican I would have won that primary  I think you have a bunch of people  running who are going to run on the pro  Trump banner and you have one person  who's saying I'm gonna stand up for the  Constitution I'm gonna stand up for the  people I represent I think when you  break it down that way it's easy to see  how I come out on top what about  President  you've talked in the past about possibly  running for president on the lp  libertarian party whatever what goes  into that calculation and where where  are you on that now well I think what  goes into the calculation is deciding  and thinking about where I can use my  skills and my influence best you know I  believe very strongly that we need  independent minded members of Congress I  feel strongly about representing my  community I love my community I love  representing my community so if I can be  most effective in that role that's what  I'll do but I also think about you know  other roles and that's why when people  ask me would you rule this out or rule  that out I don't tend to rule things out  that way it doesn't mean that I'm at a  stage where I'm gonna say yeah I'm gonna  do this for sure or I'm you know even 50  percent there but I do like to at least  consider these things  I'm stay open-minded about them and  think about how I can be most effective  and if I feel I can be effective on the  national stage spreading the message of  Liberty and the message of respect and  love then that's what I do do you have a  campaign slogan yep  you're obviously running so it's a devil  but do you have that you know I'm not  obviously ready okay all right well I  think we'll leave it there thanks so  much for talking about the reason thanks  so much now for reason I'm Nicholas  [Music]
 

